      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-16255",
      ":question/problem": "A manufacturer wishes to build a cylindrical tank with a base and a lid. The tank must have an exact volume of $100\u03c0m^{3}$.\nTo make the tank, the manufacturer uses two materials:\n\n- a metal sheet that costs $$2.50$ per $m^{2}$ for the lateral surface,\n- a metal sheet that costs $$1.50$ per $m^{2}$ for the base and lid.\n\nWhat is the radius of the tank that gives the smallest possible manufacturing cost?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
