      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-85333",
      ":question/problem": "A manufacturer wishes to build a cylindrical container with a base but no lid. The container must have an exact volume of $12\u03c0m^{3}$.\nTo make the container, the manufacturer uses two materials:\n\n- a plastic sheet that costs $$4.50$ per $m^{2}$ for the lateral surface,\n- a plastic sheet that costs $$2$ per $m^{2}$ for the base.\n\nWhat is the radius of the container that gives the smallest manufacturing cost?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
